---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DataIntegrityBlock from '../components/DataIntegrityBlock.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
});
const pageTitle = 'Our Research & Software Evaluation Methodology — The HR Stack Guide';
const pageHeading = 'Our Research & Software Evaluation Methodology';
const pageDescription =
  'The HR Stack Guide audits every platform against a 4-pillar framework covering entity architecture, total cost of ownership, administrative UX, and ecosystem integration, then rechecks pricing every 90 days.';
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  heading={pageHeading}
  description={pageDescription}
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-14">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <li><a href="/" class="transition hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true" class="text-slate-300">&gt;</li>
          <li class="font-medium text-indigo-600" aria-current="page">Methodology</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        {pageHeading}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          At The HR Stack Guide, our mission is to eliminate guesswork from B2B software procurement. We evaluate software vendors through a structured, multi-dimensional scoring framework designed to reveal operational realities that marketing materials and vendor slide decks conceal.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Every platform featured on The HR Stack Guide is audited against our proprietary <strong>4-Pillar Software Evaluation Framework</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">The 4-Pillar Software Evaluation Framework</h2>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 1: Entity &amp; Compliance Architecture (Global Payroll &amp; EOR)</h3>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            For international payroll and Employer of Record platforms, software functionality is secondary to legal and regulatory infrastructure. We evaluate:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            <li>
              <strong>Owned vs. Partner-Model Entities:</strong> Does the vendor own and operate registered local legal entities in-country, or do they route employment contracts through third-party local service providers (whitelabel EOR)? Owned infrastructure delivers faster dispute resolution, predictable onboarding timelines, and direct liability protection.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>IP Assignment &amp; Compliance Purity:</strong> How does the platform handle the chain of intellectual property transfer between international contractors/employees and your parent entity?
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Statutory Benefit Routing:</strong> Does the platform automate local country-specific mandates (e.g., 13th-month pay, mandatory pension contributions, statutory severance reserves) accurately within payroll runs?
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 2: Real-World Total Cost of Ownership (TCO)</h3>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            Sticker prices rarely reflect the true cost of operating HR software. Our pricing models uncover hidden contract fees, including:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            <li>
              <strong>Foreign Exchange (FX) &amp; Transfer Markups:</strong> We benchmark the spread vendors charge above the mid-market currency exchange rate when funding international payroll, alongside stablecoin/crypto settlement fees.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Contract Flexibility &amp; Offboarding Penalties:</strong> We evaluate deposit return timelines, minimum seat commitments, annual lock-in requirements, and employee offboarding fees.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Implementation &amp; Tiered Feature Walls:</strong> We identify critical workflow features (e.g., custom review workflows, single sign-on, advanced reporting) gated behind enterprise pricing tiers.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 3: Administrative Ergonomics &amp; Employee UX</h3>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            A feature only creates value if managers, recruiters, and employees actually adopt it without friction:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            <li>
              <strong>Self-Service Onboarding:</strong> We test employee document submission workflows, banking verification speeds, and mobile portal responsiveness.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Workflow Automation vs. Manual Interventions:</strong> Can People Operations teams automate cross-functional processes (e.g., triggering a background check upon offer acceptance) without third-party integration tools like Zapier?
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Support SLA Reliability:</strong> We analyze vendor support models, measuring dedicated account management availability, ticket response times, and real-time chat reliability during payroll cutoffs.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 4: Ecosystem Integration &amp; Data Hygiene</h3>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            No HR software operates in isolation. We analyze how effectively platforms communicate with surrounding tech stacks:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
            <li>
              <strong>Bidirectional ATS/HRIS Sync:</strong> Does candidate data map cleanly into employee profiles upon hire without duplicate entry?
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Webhook &amp; API Extensibility:</strong> Are API endpoints well-documented, rate-limited reasonably, and capable of triggering real-time webhooks for custom data warehouses?
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Security &amp; Access Governance:</strong> Verification of SOC 2 Type II compliance, GDPR alignment, ISO 27001 certifications, and granular role-based access control (RBAC).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">How Scores and Trade-offs Are Calculated</h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Our comparison ratings are quantitative evaluations across these four pillars:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>
            <strong>Category Weighting:</strong> Weightings reflect real-world buyer priorities. For example, Entity Ownership carries a 40% weighting in our EOR index, whereas Pipeline Automation carries a 35% weighting in our ATS evaluations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Persona-Specific Suitability:</strong> A platform that excels for an early-stage startup (5–25 employees) may introduce severe administrative friction for an enterprise team (500+ employees). We evaluate every tool against distinct buyer archetypes: Seed to Series B Startups, High-Volume Agencies, Scaling Mid-Market, and Distributed Multi-Country Enterprises.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Trade-Off Rule:</strong> No platform is universally “the best.” Every evaluation must explicitly state when a buyer should choose Platform A and when they should pass in favor of Platform B.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">Research Verification &amp; Audit Schedule</h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Software pricing and features change constantly. To ensure our data remains actionable:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <li>
            <strong>Quarterly Verification Cycles:</strong> Core feature tables, pricing tiers, and currency spreads are re-audited every 90 days.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Vendor Fact-Checking:</strong> We review published product documentation, API changelogs, and verified customer contracts to validate technical capabilities.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Change Log Documentation:</strong> All major comparison hubs document their last substantive audit date in the article byline.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Comparison pages are rendered as static HTML. The feature matrix, the pair-specific editorial take, and the buyer-profile summary are written into the first response, so a reader can see the trade-off without running a script. A vendor’s affiliate relationship does not change the category weightings above, and a score cannot be purchased.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          For corrections, data updates, or methodology inquiries, contact <a href="mailto:research@thehrstackguide.com" class="font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:underline">research@thehrstackguide.com</a>.
        </p>
        <DataIntegrityBlock />
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
